you can hear

31:29.000 --> 31:31.000
on CatholicInsider.com

31:31.000 --> 31:33.000
and most of the stuff you hear

31:33.000 --> 31:35.000
is nothing you'd expect from a
Catholic priest.

31:35.000 --> 31:37.000
He does all kinds of great
features

31:37.000 --> 31:40.000
like what he had recently,
debunking the Da Vinci Code.

31:40.000 --> 31:42.000
He goes on sound-seeing tours

31:42.000 --> 31:44.000
deep inside the Vatican where no
tourists

31:44.000 --> 31:46.000
or pilgrims are allowed

31:46.000 --> 31:48.000
and he's really starting to
become a big man

31:48.000 --> 31:50.000
on campus there at the Vatican.

31:50.000 --> 31:52.000
He even got Vatican Radio to
start podcasting.

31:52.000 --> 31:54.000
So on this particular show

31:54.000 --> 31:56.000
Part 1 of his Star Wars
Chronicles

31:56.000 --> 31:58.000
he talks about his

31:58.000 --> 32:00.000
his obsessiveness with the Star
Wars

32:00.000 --> 32:02.000
where it came from

32:02.000 --> 32:04.000
and there's an interesting twist
to the story

32:04.000 --> 32:06.000
at the end and if you want to
hear Part 2

32:06.000 --> 32:08.000
well you'll just have to check
out his website

32:08.000 --> 32:10.000
CatholicInsider.com

32:10.000 --> 32:12.000
but for right now here is Father
Roderick

32:12.000 --> 32:14.000
with the Catholic Insider Part 1

32:14.000 --> 32:16.000
of the Star Wars Chronicles.

32:23.750 --> 32:43.750
[ Music ]

32:46.000 --> 32:48.000
A couple of years ago

32:48.000 --> 32:50.000
I received an email from someone

32:50.000 --> 32:52.000
who worked at Skywalker Ranch.

32:52.000 --> 32:55.000
Skywalker Ranch was built by
George Lucas

32:55.000 --> 32:57.000
and a lot of the creative
departments

32:57.000 --> 32:59.000
of Lucasfilm are located there

32:59.000 --> 33:01.000
and the email said

33:01.000 --> 33:03.000
since you're coming over to the
States

33:03.000 --> 33:05.000
for the premiere of Episode 1

33:05.000 --> 33:06.000
The Phantom Manus

33:06.000 --> 33:08.000
would you like to visit the
ranch

33:08.000 --> 33:10.000
while you're in the
neighborhood?

33:10.000 --> 33:11.000
A few months later

33:11.000 --> 33:13.000
I was in California

33:13.000 --> 33:14.000
in a car

33:14.000 --> 33:15.000
driving up the lane

33:15.000 --> 33:17.000
and stopping at the security

33:17.000 --> 33:19.000
checkpoint at the entrance

33:19.000 --> 33:21.000
of Skywalker Ranch.

33:21.000 --> 33:23.000
I was about to visit the place

33:23.000 --> 33:25.000
where George Lucas was working

33:25.000 --> 33:27.000
on his Star Wars movies

33:27.000 --> 33:29.000
thousands of Star Wars fans

33:29.000 --> 33:31.000
would have happily traded in
their homes

33:31.000 --> 33:33.000
their cars, their dogs, their
wives

33:33.000 --> 33:35.000
to be able to be where I was

33:35.000 --> 33:37.000
at that moment.

33:37.000 --> 33:41.000
It was an unforgettable
experience.

33:41.000 --> 33:43.000
But let's not rush into things

33:43.000 --> 33:45.000
how did a Dutch Catholic priest

33:45.000 --> 33:47.000
working in a small village

33:47.000 --> 33:48.000
ended up there

33:48.000 --> 33:50.000
at the heart of the Star Wars
universe?

33:50.000 --> 33:52.000
And why does a Catholic priest

33:52.000 --> 33:54.000
care about Star Wars altogether?

33:54.000 --> 33:56.000
Aren't priests supposed to be
talking

33:56.000 --> 33:58.000
about heaven instead of galaxies

33:58.000 --> 34:00.000
far far away?

34:00.000 --> 34:02.000
It's against my programming to
impersonate a deity.

34:02.000 --> 34:04.000
In these Star Wars chronicles

34:04.000 --> 34:06.000
I'll tell you where my interest

34:06.000 --> 34:08.000
for George Lucas's movies came
from

34:08.000 --> 34:10.000
how Star Wars taught me

34:10.000 --> 34:12.000
how to use the power of the
internet

34:12.000 --> 34:14.000
and which adventures

34:14.000 --> 34:16.000
I experienced because of Star
Wars.

34:16.000 --> 34:18.000
Now to understand why I used

34:18.000 --> 34:20.000
to be so much into Star Wars

34:20.000 --> 34:22.000
we have to go back to

34:22.000 --> 34:24.000
my youth when I was about 8 or 9

34:24.000 --> 34:26.000
I lived at the time

34:26.000 --> 34:28.000
in a small village

34:28.000 --> 34:30.000
and I always had the idea that

34:30.000 --> 34:32.000
if there was a bright spot in
the universe

34:32.000 --> 34:34.000
I was living in the place that
was farthest from

34:34.000 --> 34:36.000
at least in my perception

34:36.000 --> 34:38.000
Now all that changed

34:38.000 --> 34:40.000
when I saw the first Star Wars
movie

34:40.000 --> 34:42.000
Now this movie

34:42.000 --> 34:44.000
was one of the first movies

34:44.000 --> 34:46.000
I ever saw in a theater

34:46.000 --> 34:48.000
in my life

34:48.000 --> 34:50.000
had an incredible impact

34:50.000 --> 34:52.000
it totally

34:52.000 --> 34:54.000
totally stunned me

34:54.000 --> 34:56.000
and I was talking only about

34:56.000 --> 34:58.000
this movie. Of course we got

34:58.000 --> 35:00.000
the toys and with my brother

35:00.000 --> 35:02.000
and my sister we would play

35:02.000 --> 35:04.000
for hours and hours each day

35:04.000 --> 35:06.000
replaying these adventures

35:06.000 --> 35:08.000
invent new adventures

35:08.000 --> 35:10.000
and I just basically

35:10.000 --> 35:12.000
collect anything that had to do

35:12.000 --> 35:14.000
with Star Wars

35:14.000 --> 35:16.000
I remember that one day

35:16.000 --> 35:18.000
at Carnival

35:18.000 --> 35:20.000
I dressed up as Luke Skywalker

35:20.000 --> 35:22.000
and I went to school

35:22.000 --> 35:24.000
in this outfit

35:24.000 --> 35:26.000
and I was totally horrified

35:26.000 --> 35:28.000
when my teacher said

35:28.000 --> 35:30.000
oh you're dressed up like this

35:30.000 --> 35:32.000
Star Trek guy

35:32.000 --> 35:34.000
and I thought like

35:34.000 --> 35:36.000
Star Trek

35:36.000 --> 35:38.000
you are supposed to be my
teacher

35:38.000 --> 35:40.000
in this school

35:40.000 --> 35:42.000
how on earth can you talk about
Star Trek

35:42.000 --> 35:44.000
when this is clearly Luke
Skywalker

35:44.000 --> 35:46.000
let alone Star Wars man

35:46.000 --> 35:48.000
where did you get your education

35:48.000 --> 35:50.000
and then most of my classmates

35:50.000 --> 35:52.000
and the other people at school

35:52.000 --> 35:54.000
didn't even know

35:54.000 --> 35:56.000
about Star Trek let alone Star
Wars

35:56.000 --> 35:58.000
but anyway

35:58.000 --> 36:00.000
I had my brother

36:00.000 --> 36:02.000
I had another couple of friends
who were also into Star Wars

36:02.000 --> 36:04.000
so for me that was

36:04.000 --> 36:06.000
like a fantastic

36:06.000 --> 36:08.000
world in my imagination

36:08.000 --> 36:10.000
and in my dreams

36:10.000 --> 36:12.000
I would travel to the stars

36:12.000 --> 36:14.000
and with these same adventures

36:14.000 --> 36:16.000
I would have my own C-3PO and
R2-D2

36:16.000 --> 36:18.000
and

36:18.000 --> 36:20.000
it was a great inspiration

36:20.000 --> 36:22.000
for all the games we played

36:22.000 --> 36:24.000
and all the adventures we kind
of invented

36:24.000 --> 36:26.000
playing with the toys etc

36:26.000 --> 36:28.000
now don't get me wrong

36:28.000 --> 36:30.000
I don't have anything against
Star Trek

36:30.000 --> 36:32.000
actually

36:32.000 --> 36:34.000
I was very fascinated

36:34.000 --> 36:36.000
by Star Trek we couldn't get
that

36:36.000 --> 36:38.000
on Dutch television

36:38.000 --> 36:40.000
but from time to time

36:40.000 --> 36:42.000
we went over to stay at

36:42.000 --> 36:44.000
our grandparents place

36:44.000 --> 36:46.000
and they were living in the
south

36:46.000 --> 36:48.000
of the country

36:48.000 --> 36:50.000
on their television they could
receive

36:50.000 --> 36:52.000
German television

36:52.000 --> 36:54.000
and I remember that I used to
watch

36:54.000 --> 36:56.000
their black and white television

36:56.000 --> 36:58.000
and they would show these
episodes

36:58.000 --> 37:00.000
of Star Trek

37:00.000 --> 37:02.000
and they dubbed it in German

37:02.000 --> 37:04.000
and of course I didn't
understand a word of it

37:04.000 --> 37:06.000
but I thought it was great

37:06.000 --> 37:08.000
I clearly remember

37:08.000 --> 37:10.000
Doctor Spock

37:10.000 --> 37:12.000
now we would say hokey special
effects

37:12.000 --> 37:14.000
but at the time I thought it was

37:14.000 --> 37:16.000
just fantastic

37:16.000 --> 37:18.000
this series

37:18.000 --> 37:20.000
about stars

37:20.000 --> 37:22.000
about a starship that would
travel to the stars

37:22.000 --> 37:24.000
about aliens

37:24.000 --> 37:26.000
just totally fantastic

37:26.000 --> 37:28.000
that alone was worth

37:28.000 --> 37:30.000
making the trip to my
grandparents

37:30.000 --> 37:32.000
it was fantastic

37:32.000 --> 37:34.000
but Star Wars was still
something

37:34.000 --> 37:36.000
that sparked even more

37:36.000 --> 37:38.000
my imagination

37:38.000 --> 37:40.000
Star Wars and Star Trek

37:40.000 --> 37:42.000
also to a lesser extent

37:42.000 --> 37:44.000
also sparked my interest for
astronomy

37:44.000 --> 37:46.000
and I used to have

37:46.000 --> 37:48.000
in my room all these model kits

37:48.000 --> 37:50.000
of space crafts

37:50.000 --> 37:52.000
of the space shuttle

37:52.000 --> 37:54.000
I used to make these little
planets

37:54.000 --> 37:56.000
of round balls

37:56.000 --> 37:58.000
I would paint them and I would
hang them

37:58.000 --> 38:00.000
a little cord

38:00.000 --> 38:02.000
like that on the ceiling

38:02.000 --> 38:04.000
so my whole room looked like

38:04.000 --> 38:06.000
observatory actually

38:06.000 --> 38:08.000
and then after a long long time

38:08.000 --> 38:10.000
finally we had the second

38:10.000 --> 38:12.000
Star Wars movie and it was even

38:12.000 --> 38:14.000
even better than the first one

38:14.000 --> 38:16.000
and of course I was older so I
understood the story

38:16.000 --> 38:18.000
a little bit more

38:18.000 --> 38:20.000
and that was just fantastic

38:20.000 --> 38:22.000
and of course I was kind of

38:22.000 --> 38:24.000
shocked that Luke

38:24.000 --> 38:26.000
didn't get involved with Leia

38:26.000 --> 38:28.000
but that Han Solo actually got
the princess

38:30.000 --> 38:32.000
I found that very shocking

38:32.000 --> 38:34.000
Luke Skywalker was my hero

38:34.000 --> 38:36.000
and Han Solo was just this

38:36.000 --> 38:38.000
kind of wild guy

38:38.000 --> 38:40.000
he just didn't deserve princess
Leia

38:40.000 --> 38:42.000
that was my opinion at the time

38:42.000 --> 38:44.000
and the third movie came out

38:44.000 --> 38:46.000
I was even older and that was
also

38:46.000 --> 38:48.000
a fantastic conclusion

38:48.000 --> 38:50.000
to the whole saga

38:50.000 --> 38:52.000
and then of course we got our
first video recorder

38:52.000 --> 38:54.000
and I bought these movies on
video

38:54.000 --> 38:56.000
and I would play them

38:56.000 --> 38:58.000
over and over again

38:58.000 --> 39:00.000
I must have seen a hundred times

39:00.000 --> 39:02.000
a total waste of time perhaps

39:02.000 --> 39:04.000
for some people but for me

39:04.000 --> 39:06.000
it was just like reading my
favorite book

39:06.000 --> 39:08.000
I would read it over and over
again

39:08.000 --> 39:10.000
and it was the same with these
movies

39:10.000 --> 39:12.000
so I knew them all by heart

39:12.000 --> 39:14.000
I wasn't the only one because my
brother

39:14.000 --> 39:16.000
had the same geeky behavior

39:16.000 --> 39:18.000
so we were used to

39:18.000 --> 39:20.000
when we were washing the dishes

39:20.000 --> 39:22.000
we used to kind of recite the
whole movie together

39:22.000 --> 39:24.000
so when I was about 17 or 18

39:24.000 --> 39:26.000
I started to rediscover

39:26.000 --> 39:28.000
my faith and

39:28.000 --> 39:30.000
when I was in that process

39:30.000 --> 39:32.000
I also started to

39:32.000 --> 39:34.000
discover that there was actually

39:34.000 --> 39:36.000
a second layer in these Star
Wars movies

39:36.000 --> 39:38.000
it wasn't just a popcorn story

39:38.000 --> 39:40.000
about a princess

39:40.000 --> 39:42.000
about Luke Skywalker

39:42.000 --> 39:44.000
some spaceships and some space
wars

39:44.000 --> 39:46.000
but that there were

39:46.000 --> 39:48.000
a lot of mythological

39:48.000 --> 39:50.000
also religious themes

39:50.000 --> 39:52.000
that church Lucas took

39:52.000 --> 39:54.000
and put them in the story

39:54.000 --> 39:56.000
of the movie

39:56.000 --> 39:58.000
I also started reading about
this

39:58.000 --> 40:00.000
it was actually

40:00.000 --> 40:02.000
something that George Lucas did
deliberately

40:02.000 --> 40:04.000
because he said

40:04.000 --> 40:06.000
he wanted to create

40:06.000 --> 40:08.000
a new mythology for young people

40:08.000 --> 40:10.000
for today's young people

40:10.000 --> 40:12.000
to talk to them

40:12.000 --> 40:14.000
to teach them about good

40:14.000 --> 40:16.000
and evil about the consequences

40:16.000 --> 40:18.000
of our choices

40:18.000 --> 40:20.000
and I was fascinated

40:20.000 --> 40:22.000
by that deeper level

40:22.000 --> 40:24.000
of the movie and I started to
read

40:24.000 --> 40:26.000
about it and start to

40:26.000 --> 40:28.000
rediscover these movies

40:28.000 --> 40:30.000
and so they became even more

40:30.000 --> 40:32.000
intriguing and more interesting

40:32.000 --> 40:34.000
so I also

40:34.000 --> 40:36.000
tried to find out the
differences

40:36.000 --> 40:38.000
between the kind of

40:38.000 --> 40:40.000
philosophy that you find in Star
Wars

40:40.000 --> 40:42.000
and the

40:42.000 --> 40:44.000
philosophy of faith

40:44.000 --> 40:46.000
of the Catholic faith and the
values in there

40:46.000 --> 40:48.000
it made me look at these movies
over and over again

40:48.000 --> 40:50.000
trying to

40:50.000 --> 40:52.000
see all these links and
references

40:52.000 --> 40:54.000
and also the whole

40:54.000 --> 40:56.000
trilogy itself had so many

40:56.000 --> 40:58.000
internal references

40:58.000 --> 41:00.000
and I just rediscovered

41:00.000 --> 41:02.000
how very very well constructed
these stories were

41:02.000 --> 41:04.000
and that is also

41:04.000 --> 41:06.000
for me

41:06.000 --> 41:08.000
why they worked and why they
worked on a global level

41:08.000 --> 41:10.000
because

41:10.000 --> 41:12.000
George Lucas didn't only want to
make

41:12.000 --> 41:14.000
a popcorn movie

41:14.000 --> 41:16.000
but he just inserted all these

41:16.000 --> 41:18.000
mythological themes

41:18.000 --> 41:20.000
and kind of the core

41:20.000 --> 41:22.000
themes of storytelling

41:22.000 --> 41:24.000
so that would actually

41:24.000 --> 41:26.000
kind of evoke

41:26.000 --> 41:28.000
the central themes

41:28.000 --> 41:30.000
in a lot of cultures and a lot
of

41:30.000 --> 41:32.000
philosophies and in a lot of
religions

41:32.000 --> 41:34.000
I studied for 10 years

41:34.000 --> 41:36.000
in order to become

41:36.000 --> 41:38.000
a priest I first did 4 years

41:38.000 --> 41:40.000
of philosophy and then

41:40.000 --> 41:42.000
I did another year of theology

41:42.000 --> 41:44.000
I did all that in Belgium

41:44.000 --> 41:46.000
then I did another 5 years of

41:46.000 --> 41:48.000
theology in Holland in Utrecht

41:48.000 --> 41:50.000
and then I was ordained

41:50.000 --> 41:52.000
and after my ordination

41:52.000 --> 41:54.000
my bishop asked me to work

41:54.000 --> 41:56.000
for 50% in a couple of parishes

41:56.000 --> 41:58.000
and then for 50% to start

41:58.000 --> 42:00.000
a doctorate

42:00.000 --> 42:02.000
on the theology of

42:02.000 --> 42:04.000
Saint Thomas Aquinas

42:04.000 --> 42:06.000
a very important medieval

42:06.000 --> 42:08.000
theologian and philosopher

42:08.000 --> 42:10.000
and while I was starting

42:10.000 --> 42:12.000
my studies at university

42:12.000 --> 42:14.000
I first got into contact with

42:14.000 --> 42:16.000
the internet

42:16.000 --> 42:18.000
and one thing that at the time
was relatively new

42:18.000 --> 42:20.000
we didn't have it

42:20.000 --> 42:22.000
at home so what I did

42:22.000 --> 42:24.000
was in my free time I was kind
of

42:24.000 --> 42:26.000
surfing the internet and
discovering

42:26.000 --> 42:28.000
all these different topics

42:28.000 --> 42:30.000
that people made websites about

42:30.000 --> 42:32.000
and one thing I discovered

42:32.000 --> 42:34.000
was a website about Star Wars

42:34.000 --> 42:36.000
that told me that you know

42:36.000 --> 42:38.000
George Lucas was going to make
the prequels

42:38.000 --> 42:40.000
so new Star Wars movies

42:40.000 --> 42:42.000
and suddenly this whole

42:42.000 --> 42:44.000
enthusiasm for Star Wars

42:44.000 --> 42:46.000
just know everything about it

42:46.000 --> 42:48.000
so I started looking for the
rumors

42:48.000 --> 42:50.000
about these new movies and when
they would be

42:50.000 --> 42:52.000
filmed and you know I was most

42:52.000 --> 42:54.000
of course very much interested

42:54.000 --> 42:56.000
in the storyline you know

42:56.000 --> 42:58.000
how can you make prequels what
are they going to be about

42:58.000 --> 43:00.000
and of course this storyline

43:00.000 --> 43:02.000
was ultra secret

43:02.000 --> 43:04.000
but I started to

43:04.000 --> 43:06.000
gather on the internet

43:06.000 --> 43:08.000
all the little rumors

43:08.000 --> 43:10.000
and little you know leaked out
secrets

43:10.000 --> 43:12.000
of this new movie

43:12.000 --> 43:14.000
and I started to put them

43:14.000 --> 43:16.000
on a website

43:16.000 --> 43:18.000
and that started off

43:18.000 --> 43:20.000
a whole new adventure for me

43:20.000 --> 43:22.000
on the internet and I will tell
you more

43:22.000 --> 43:24.000
about it in the next episode

43:24.000 --> 43:26.000
of the Star Wars Chronicles

43:42.000 --> 43:44.000
the past weeks podcasting
activity

43:44.000 --> 43:46.000
and some of the news stories
that popped up

43:46.000 --> 43:48.000
on the radar

